  "data_abstract": "A search for magnetic monopoles is presented using 0.262 nb$^{-1}$ of Run 3 ultraperipheral Pb+Pb collision (UPC) data at $\\sqrt{s_{\\textrm{NN}}}=5.36$ TeV collected by the ATLAS detector at the LHC. By exploiting the properties of clusters reconstructed in the innermost silicon detector layers, a new methodology for studying highly ionizing particles in heavy-ion data at the LHC is introduced. Using a non-perturbative semiclassical model, upper limits are set on the cross-section for pair production of monopoles with a single Dirac magnetic charge in the mass range of 20--150 GeV. The search improves the previous cross-section limits for production of monopoles with masses below 120 GeV in Pb+Pb UPC.",
